        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "58ab406b-97f0-50c5-8155-c925d98abbdf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Il trovatore, La rondine, Rigoletto, Elena da Feltre, El trovador\n- People: Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez, Giacomo Puccini, Giuseppe Adami, Alfred Maria Willner, Pietro Neri-Baraldi\n- Organizations: Teatro del Corso\n- Places: Bologna\n- Roles: Manrico, Duke of Mantua, Ubaldo, leading tenor\n\nFacts:\n- In 1836, Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the play \"El trovador.\"\n- Il trovatore is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano and based on Antonio García Gutiérrez's 1836 play \"El trovador.\"\n- By 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi was engaged as the leading tenor at the Teatro del Corso.\n- By 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi sang Manrico in the first Bologna performance of Il trovatore at the Teatro del Corso.\n- By 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi sang the Duke of Mantua in the first Bologna performance of Rigoletto at the Teatro del Corso.\n- By 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi sang Ubaldo in the first Bologna performance of Elena da Feltre at the Teatro del Corso.\n- La rondine is an opera in three acts by Giacomo Puccini with an Italian libretto by Giuseppe Adami based on a libretto by Alfred Maria Willner.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
